/* book exam traps: Multiplying VA by hours and calling it stored energy. Apparent power must pass through the load power factor and the inverter efficiency before it becomes battery watts. | Using battery Ah × voltage as backup time without depth of discharge and inverter efficiency. A 100 Ah battery is not 100 Ah of usable energy. | Choosing a UPS only by watts. The UPS VA rating must exceed load VA, because current heats the inverter and transformer. | Thinking every UPS has the same transfer time. Off-line and line-interactive types switch the load; on-line double conversion does not transfer the load on mains failure. | Forgetting that a lead-acid block delivers fewer Ah at a high rate. A 30-minute UPS discharge gets only a part of the 20-hour Ah printed on the block, so use the maker's table. */
