/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A work coil carries a high-frequency AC current and creates an alternating magnetic field.
   - δ = √(ρ / (π f μ))
   - δ is skin depth in m; ρ is workpiece resistivity in Ω·m; f is coil current frequency in Hz; μ is workpiece permeability in H/m, equal to μr μ0.
   - Below the Curie point (about 770 °C) magnetic steel has μr of about 100 and ρ of about 2 × 10⁻⁷ Ω·m, so δ is only 3.2 mm at 50 Hz and 0.23 mm at 10 kHz.
   - A resonant inverter converts DC to the coil frequency.
   - Power is set by frequency or DC link.
*/
