/* book exam traps: Using the skin depth of cold magnetic steel for the whole cycle. Above the Curie point δ becomes about 25 times larger at the same frequency, so the frequency is chosen for hot steel. | Thinking the coil makes most of the heat; the coil is water-cooled and the heat is in the workpiece. | Forgetting the reflected resistance and low power factor; coil current is not P/V, it is P/(V × pf). | Treating the Curie point as a fixed number; above it μr falls sharply and δ, Rref and power all change. | Designing the tank at one load only; cold, hot and molten workpieces change the resonant frequency and coupling. */
